turnkey-sysinfo (1.1.0+keel2) trixie; urgency=medium

  * The login message says "Welcome to keel-web1, Keel Linux 19.0 (Debian
    13/Trixie)". contrib/motd took its welcome line from
    sysversion.fmt_sysversion, which names TurnKey GNU/Linux and which the
    turnkey-version fork leaves alone; the line is now composed here, in
    libsysinfo/welcome.py: the release from /etc/keel_version, with
    /etc/turnkey_version as the fallback (common, decision 0014; an app name
    with hyphens is parsed from the right), the base distribution from
    lsb_release as before, and the same fallbacks as upstream when one or
    both are missing. The hostname is printed as the machine has it:
    upstream's str.capitalize() made keel-web1 "Keel-web1".
  * debian/control describes a Keel Linux server. The copyright headers,
    the package and command names, and the TKLBAM block of turnkey-sysinfo
    (common's motd drop-in leaves it out; whether an appliance ships TKLBAM
    is handbook#6) are untouched.
  * tests/test_welcome.py, run by pybuild at build time (python3-pytest in
    Build-Depends), so the package check exercises it.

 -- Keel Linux maintainers <admin@keellinux.org>  Fri, 03 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000

turnkey-sysinfo (1.1.0+keel1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Build for Keel Linux, Debian 13.
  * Build-Depends: python3-setuptools, the build backend pyproject.toml
    names (setuptools.build_meta); on a bare trixie the wheel build fails
    without it (as turnkey-netinfo did).

 -- Keel Linux maintainers <admin@keellinux.org>  Fri, 02 Oct 2026 17:40:52 +0000
